# Copy to .env and adjust. Loaded by the Nix dev shell and by every `just`
# recipe (`set dotenv-load`). Keep secrets out of git -- .env is ignored.
#
# Secrets: give them a placeholder value starting with `change-me-`, e.g.
#   SESSION_SECRET=change-me-generated-on-first-shell
# and `nix develop` replaces it in .env with `openssl rand -hex 32` once.

# Where the dev shell installs the Android SDK and the mobile build looks for
# it. Leave unset to use ~/Android/Sdk (Android Studio's default).
# ANDROID_HOME=/home/you/Android/Sdk

# Set to 0 to stop the dev shell from installing the Android SDK on entry
# (desktop-only work, CI).
# ANDROID_SDK_INSTALL=0

# Host the Vite dev server listens on, so a phone or emulator can reach the
# desktop's dev server. Leave unset for localhost only.
# TAURI_DEV_HOST=192.168.1.10
